WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.140
- When the book was released,

00:00:01.140 --> 00:00:04.350
a lot of people kind of made
it about a coming out party,

00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:05.183
story for you,

00:00:05.183 --> 00:00:06.920
but that wasn't really
why you made the book.

00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:07.753
Right?

00:00:07.753 --> 00:00:11.490
- I am very naive in how I
tell my story in the sense that

00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:13.450
putting this book together
for four and a half years.

00:00:13.450 --> 00:00:15.940
To me, I thought the
most interesting story

00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:18.610
about my journey is being a young man of

00:00:18.610 --> 00:00:21.180
color in Hollywood and
navigating what that's like.

00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:23.120
And then finally getting
the chance to work

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:24.830
in the industry I love.

00:00:24.830 --> 00:00:26.380
Going to work for the
first black president of

00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:27.213
The United States.

00:00:27.213 --> 00:00:28.464
What's that like.

00:00:28.464 --> 00:00:30.867
- And like also just coming
from entertainment industry

00:00:30.867 --> 00:00:34.470
and making that move and then
still being a part of it,

00:00:34.470 --> 00:00:35.370
that's interesting.

00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:38.010
- So I am just so excited to
share that full breath of my

00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:39.827
experiences and story with people

00:00:39.827 --> 00:00:40.676
and it's been really fun

00:00:40.676 --> 00:00:43.040
to write and get the
whole thing out there.

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:45.020
- I love that. I think four
years, that's so much time.

00:00:45.020 --> 00:00:45.853
So it's like your baby,

00:00:45.853 --> 00:00:47.960
but I love that you showed
every different kind of

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:48.793
part of your life.

00:00:48.793 --> 00:00:50.340
I think that's really
cool and it lets people in

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:52.790
and also inspires people
that you can dream big

00:00:52.790 --> 00:00:54.460
and you can make it happen. I love that.

00:00:54.460 --> 00:00:55.951
- Thank you.

00:00:55.951 --> 00:00:59.490
My two goals When I was
putting the book together,

00:00:59.490 --> 00:01:00.440
I said I want to write a book

00:01:00.440 --> 00:01:02.490
for the 25 year-old version of me.

00:01:02.490 --> 00:01:03.810
The kid who's like trying to figure out

00:01:03.810 --> 00:01:04.700
how to make things work.

00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:05.847
And there's no guidebook for that.

00:01:05.847 --> 00:01:08.470
And I also want to write it
for the person who's out there

00:01:08.470 --> 00:01:09.810
who has multiple passions, right?

00:01:09.810 --> 00:01:11.740
Who doesn't view the world as binary or

00:01:11.740 --> 00:01:13.470
doesn't view things as mutually exclusive

00:01:13.470 --> 00:01:15.220
and says, I like this and that

00:01:15.220 --> 00:01:16.340
and maybe I'm going to take a chance.

00:01:16.340 --> 00:01:18.690
Maybe I'm going to do that
crazy thing that everybody said

00:01:18.690 --> 00:01:20.700
you shouldn't do because it's crazy.

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:22.800
Especially
- You only live once, why not?

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:23.633
- You only live once,

00:01:23.633 --> 00:01:24.510
especially through the pandemic.

00:01:24.510 --> 00:01:25.610
So many people realized,

00:01:25.610 --> 00:01:27.120
wait, I don't like what I'm doing now or

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:28.430
I want to add that other thing.

00:01:28.430 --> 00:01:29.860
So this story is also for them

00:01:29.860 --> 00:01:32.380
and sharing my experiences
with all of that stuff.

00:01:32.380 --> 00:01:33.213
- And that's so true,

00:01:33.213 --> 00:01:34.250
Everybody did like you kind of,

00:01:34.250 --> 00:01:36.188
I literally just was texting
last night with with a friend,

00:01:36.188 --> 00:01:37.021
I was like,

00:01:37.021 --> 00:01:39.340
I literally have regular
talks with my therapist.

00:01:39.340 --> 00:01:41.353
I'm just like wait, I'm
doing what I love, Right?

00:01:41.353 --> 00:01:42.186
And I am doing what I love,

00:01:42.186 --> 00:01:43.019
but you have that conversation like

00:01:43.019 --> 00:01:44.360
if I had a year to live,
what would I be doing?

00:01:44.360 --> 00:01:46.250
Like, you know, I always have
this conversation and it is

00:01:46.250 --> 00:01:48.170
I think that COVID did
that to a lot of us.

00:01:48.170 --> 00:01:50.500
It made us really like
question the time we spend with

00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:53.190
each other and like what,
are really doing we love?

00:01:53.190 --> 00:01:54.430
which I do love what I'm doing.

00:01:54.430 --> 00:01:55.800
- Same, I feel so lucky

00:01:55.800 --> 00:01:57.677
- Yeah, I know I'm super glad

